BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:censys@2026-10-28@internet-security-snapshot
DTSTAMP:20261024T000000Z
DTSTART:20261028T180000Z
DTEND:20261028T190000Z
SUMMARY:[Paul] Snapshot: Write and send the Censys research-access applicat
 ion
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Paul (author)\n\nMoved from 15 Feb 2027 (17 Nov\, 
 then 28 Oct at the author's choice). In your own words: Censys rejects req
 uests written with AI tools\, and the standing rules say you write it. It 
 is an email to research-access-request@censys.com (no web form) covering: 
 a 3-4 sentence project description with the research question and where re
 sults are published\; your background (public profile or past work)\; how 
 Censys helps and which access (BigQuery\; delayed data is fine)\; how rece
 nt the data must be\; confirmation of non-commercial use and citing Censys
 \; agreement to the terms\; your Censys username (make an account first). 
 Guide: Claude doc "Censys Research Access: Application Guide". Log it in h
 ttps://github.com/pagagne/internet-security-snapshot/blob/main/docs/PERMIS
 SIONS.md (Claude can do the log). Access to choose: option 3 on their page
 \, additional API endpoints and Censys credits (counts by software version
  or CVE without host data\; enough credits for weekly counts on about 80-1
 00 flaws a quarter\, a few hundred count queries a month). Not raw Parquet
  downloads (too large\; host data). Platform UI optional. Two things to as
 k: (1) can count queries be run as of past dates\, back to late 2025\, for
  a baseline year? (2) is BigQuery access also available? It would run in t
 he Google Cloud project set up on 29 Oct.\n\nSource: https://github.com/pa
 gagne/internet-security-snapshot/blob/main/docs/schedule/schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:Author
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gcp-setup@2026-10-29@internet-security-snapshot
DTSTAMP:20261024T000000Z
DTSTART:20261029T140000Z
DTEND:20261029T142000Z
SUMMARY:[Paul] Snapshot: Set up BigQuery in the Google Cloud project (HTTP 
 Archive\, deps.dev history)\; turn on Dependabot alerts
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Paul (author)\n\nFirst\, one minute in GitHub (ste
 p 3 of the 27 Oct settings PDF): Settings > Advanced Security > Dependabot
  alerts > Enable (dependency graph on\; security and version updates left 
 off)\; tell Claude\, who checks it. The project "internet-security-snapsho
 t" already exists (made 27 Oct for the Drive backup's client ID). console.
 cloud.google.com\, that project: enable the BigQuery API\; no billing need
 ed (the BigQuery sandbox includes 1 TB of queries a month)\; if you ever l
 ink billing\, add a budget alert at $1\; IAM > Service accounts > create "
 snapshot-bq" with the role BigQuery Job User\; Keys > Add key > JSON\; in 
 GitHub > Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions\, add GCP_SA_KEY (past
 e the whole file) and GCP_PROJECT (the project ID). Never paste the key in
 to chat. Delete the downloaded file afterwards.\n\nSource: https://github.
 com/pagagne/internet-security-snapshot/blob/main/docs/schedule/schedule.ya
 ml
CATEGORIES:Author
END:VEVENT
