SUMMARY:[Claude] Snapshot: HTTP Archive test - are software versions record
 ed? (after the BigQuery project)
DESCRIPTION:Responsible: Claude\n\nOne small BigQuery query within the free
  tier\, with a per-query byte cap. If versions are recorded\, propose an e
 xploratory patch-adoption measure for web software (share of sites on the 
 fixed version\, 30 and 90 days after the fix). WordPress.org version stati
 stics work (probe 25 Oct: version shares per plugin\, today only)\, so the
 y need weekly capture to build history. Also deps.dev's BigQuery history f
 or the patch-adoption prototype. First test case: PHP2Shell (fixed 21 Oct 
 2026\; author's concern of 26 Oct that many servers will stay unpatched): 
 from the X-Powered-By PHP versions in the September\, October and November
  crawls\, the share of PHP-reporting sites on a fixed release\, and the sh
 are on releases that will never get a fix (PHP 5.4-7.3). Sites that hide t
 heir version are not counted.\n\nSource: https://github.com/pagagne/intern
 et-security-snapshot/blob/main/docs/schedule/schedule.yaml
CATEGORIES:Claude
END:VEVENT
